---
title: Hyderabadi Vegetable Biryani
portions: 6
category: Rice
source: "https://www.cinnamonsnail.com/vegan-biryani/"
---

## Rice

[Soak] Soak the @basmati-rice{200 g}, ~{30 min}. Rinse under cold water and drain.

[Toast] Heat the @olive-oil{15 ml} in a #saucepan{} over high heat. Fry the @cloves{} and the @cardamom{1 g}, ~{30 s}.

[Steam] Add the drained rice and toast, stirring, ~{60 s}. Pour in the @water{360 ml}, cover, and when boiling reduce to low. Steam until the rice is cooked and all water is absorbed, ~{18 min}.

## Vegetables

[Boil] Meanwhile, boil the diced @potato{180 g} and @carrot{60 g} in a #pot{} of salted water until fork-tender, ~{13 min}. Drain.

[Sauté] Melt the @vegan-butter{43 g} in a large #skillet{} over medium-high heat. Sauté the @cauliflower{150 g}(florets), the @green-beans{120 g}(chopped), the @green-chili{15 g}(minced) and the @ginger{8 g}(grated), ~{5 min}.

[Spice] Add the @cumin{1.5 g}, the @turmeric{3 g}, the @chili-powder{2 g}(Kashmiri) and the @curry-leaves{}. Stir to coat, ~{1 min}.

[Simmer] Stir in the chopped @tomato{150 g}, the @peas{90 g} and the boiled potato and carrot. Cover and cook over low heat until the vegetables are tender, ~{10 min}.

[Layer] Fluff the rice with a fork and fold it through the vegetables along with the @cashews{50 g}(toasted).

[Finish] Sprinkle with @rosewater{2.5 ml}.

## Serve

[Serve] Garnish with fresh @cilantro{} and @mint{}. Serve hot.
